B.Yb=new A.bP(B.yr,["You are checking a photo for a Korean app that ranks winter puffer jackets (\ud328\ub529) by brand.\n1. Decide whether the photo shows a padded/down/insulated outer jacket or coat, or a garment tag/label from one. If it does not (e.g. a fleece, a T-shirt, a person without such a jacket, a random object), set isTarget to false and name to null.\n2. If it does, identify the brand from logos, patches, zipper pulls, tags/labels and distinctive design, and choose exactly one name from the candidate list. Copy the candidate string exactly as written.\n3. If the brand cannot be determined with reasonable certainty, or it is not in the list, set name to null. Do not guess from colour or silhouette alone.\n4. Sub-lines matter: \uc544\ud06c\ud14c\ub9ad\uc2a4 vs \uc544\ud06c\ud14c\ub9ad\uc2a4 \ubca0\uc77c\ub7f0\uc2a4, \ubabd\ud074\ub808\ub974 vs \ubabd\ud074\ub808\ub974 \uadf8\ub974\ub178\ube14, \ub178\uc2a4\ud398\uc774\uc2a4 vs \ub178\uc2a4\ud398\uc774\uc2a4 \ud654\uc774\ud2b8\ub77c\ubca8. Pick the sub-line only when its own label or logo is visible.\n5. confidence is your probability (0 to 1) that the chosen name is correct; when name is null, give your confidence that the isTarget judgement is correct."],t.li)
